/* Backup Overview - the full page.
 *
 * Rendering lives in overview.php, shared with overview-poll.php which serves the
 * refresh, so first paint and updates come from one code path.
 *
 * This is deliberately NOT a row of KPI cards. Those look like a dashboard but
 * earn little: "5 datasets / 2 missing / 60%" still leaves you scanning the table
 * to find out which two. The page has a whole screen, so it spends it on three
 * facts stated outright, the transfer in its own section, and then the datasets -
 * using the same dots, colours, wording and provider order as the tile, from the
 * same bo_mark() and bo_pal().
 *
 * Refresh model:
 *   every 1s   overview-live.php  - transfer figures, patched in place
 *   every 30s  overview-poll.php  - the whole panel
 * Which rows are expanded is held OUTSIDE the DOM and re-applied after each
 * rebuild, because the 30s tick replaces every node - state stored only in those
 * nodes gets thrown away and rows collapse on their own seconds after you open
 * them, which is what happened on the tile before it was fixed.
 */
require_once '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/backup-widget/overview.php';
?>
